# Protect an API on the APIM gateway with AM access tokens

This guide has a backend service call an API published on the Gravitee APIM gateway, with an access token from
AM. The service gets the token from the AM gateway (OAuth 2.0 client credentials), and the APIM gateway checks it
on every call. One Terraform configuration holds both sides: AM with this provider, APIM with the
[`gravitee-io/apim`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/gravitee-io/apim/latest/docs) provider.

## Before you start

* The AM provider reaches the AM Automation API with `AM_SERVER_URL` and a service-account token in
  `AM_SA_TOKEN`; the APIM provider reaches the APIM Automation API with `APIM_SERVER_URL` and `APIM_SA_TOKEN`.
* Terraform 1.11 or later: the client secret values are write-only attributes.
* The APIM gateway reaches the AM gateway. The configuration reads its URL from the `gateway_url` of the domain's
  data plane.

Both providers, in `provider.tf`:

```terraform
terraform {
  # Write-only attributes, such as the value_wo of am_client_secret, need Terraform 1.11 or later.
  required_version = ">= 1.11"
  required_providers {
    am = {
      source = "gravitee-io/am"
    }
    apim = {
      source = "gravitee-io/apim"
    }
  }
}

provider "am" {}
provider "apim" {}
```

